(ServiceHub Backend: What Is in Place) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In one sentence) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This began as the starter structure for ServiceHub and now includes the first working) Tj
T*
(account and business-membership flows. A scaffold is the foundation of a project; the later) Tj
T*
(feature modules are still being built on it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What works today) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The server starts with `npm run dev`.) Tj
T*
(- `GET /api/v1/health` responds with `{ "status": "ok" }`.) Tj
T*
(- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` creates a user, a business, and an owner membership in one) Tj
T*
(transaction.) Tj
T*
(- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` checks the password and returns a 15-minute bearer access token.) Tj
T*
(- `GET /api/v1/auth/me` returns the signed-in user and their business memberships.) Tj
T*
(- `GET /api/v1/businesses/current` returns the active business selected from a verified) Tj
T*
(membership.) Tj
T*
(- Passwords are stored using Node.js scrypt hashes; registration and login have a stricter) Tj
T*
(rate limit.) Tj
T*
(- The health endpoint has an automated test. The test suite has not yet been rerun after the) Tj
T*
(auth changes.) Tj
T*
(- Environment settings are checked with Zod when the app starts.) Tj
T*
(- Requests are logged, common security headers are set, CORS and JSON parsing are) Tj
T*
(configured, and API requests are rate limited.) Tj
T*
(- Errors go through one handler and use a consistent JSON shape: `{ "error": { "code":) Tj
T*
("...", "message": "..." } }`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(How the folders are organized) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `src/app.js` assembles Express middleware and routes. `src/server.js` starts the listening) Tj
T*
(server.) Tj
T*
(- `src/config/` validates settings. `src/middlewares/` includes authentication, tenant) Tj
T*
(membership, RBAC, request validation, rate limiting, and error handling.) Tj
T*
(- `src/modules/auth/` implements registration, login, and current-user profile.) Tj
T*
(`src/modules/businesses/` implements the current business route and membership lookup.) Tj
T*
(- `src/modules/` also contains placeholder modules for users, services, staff, schedules,) Tj
T*
(appointments, reviews, notifications, dashboard, audit logs, and platform admin.) Tj
T*
(- `src/database/` contains the Prisma client setup and transaction helper.) Tj
T*
(`prisma/schema.prisma` and the initial migration define users, businesses, and memberships.) Tj
T*
(- `src/lib/`, `src/jobs/`, and `src/realtime/` hold placeholders for logging, Redis/BullMQ) Tj
T*
(jobs, and Socket.IO.) Tj
T*
(- `tests/` contains the health endpoint test. `docs/` describes architecture, API) Tj
T*
(conventions, and tenancy guidance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What is not built yet) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Password reset, email verification, refresh tokens, session revocation, and broader user and) Tj
T*
(business management are not implemented. Service, staff, schedule, appointment, review,) Tj
T*
(notification, dashboard, audit-log, and platform-admin features remain placeholders. Redis,) Tj
T*
(BullMQ, and Socket.IO are not connected yet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
