(Tenant design) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The design uses one shared PostgreSQL database. The current tenant middleware checks an) Tj
T*
(authenticated user's membership and active business status before attaching `req.tenant`. It) Tj
T*
(accepts `X-Business-Id` for users with multiple memberships. Future tenant-owned tables) Tj
T*
(should include `businessId`, and each repository query should filter by that verified ID.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Run it locally) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Requires Node.js 22 or newer. From the project folder:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Run `npm install`.) Tj
T*
(2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set `DATABASE_URL` and a private `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET`.) Tj
T*
(3. Apply the initial migration with `npm run prisma:deploy`.) Tj
T*
(4. Run `npm run dev`.) Tj
T*
(5. Open `http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health` or call the auth routes with an API client.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(PostgreSQL must be running for registration, login, profile, and business routes. Redis is) Tj
T*
(only a configuration value for now; the app does not connect to it yet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Suggested build order) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Complete user and business management, including password reset and email verification.) Tj
T*
(2. Services and staff.) Tj
T*
(3. Schedules.) Tj
T*
(4. Appointments.) Tj
T*
(5. Reviews, notifications, dashboard, audit logs, and platform administration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
